# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing derived from the retail game may be committed to this repository.
#
# Everything the game needs is read off YOUR copy of the disc at run time, or
# materialised into build/ from it (see docs/ASSETS.md). None of it is
# redistributable, and none of it belongs in this history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build output
/burnout3
*.o
/dist/

# The corrected ELF and every materialised asset: geometry, textures, audio,
# music, collision, the per-track binaries and the ISO cache. Several GB once a
# full extraction has run; nothing here is committed.
#   burnout3.elf   : tools/xbe2elf.py
#   everything else: tools/cextract (in process, on a cache miss)
/build/

# THE EIGHT PURGED HEADERS -- a tripwire, not a build product.
#
# These used to bake retail data into src/: the vehicle roster, per-car tuning,
# the fonts, track paths, start grids, AI pace, traffic sets and the Globalus
# display strings. All eight are GONE, replaced by src/*_runtime.h loaders that
# read the user's own files at boot, and tools/validate_no_baked_data.py fails
# if any of them comes back. They are listed here so that an old tree, or an
# archived generator run by hand, cannot quietly re-commit one.
/src/burnout3_ai_pace.h
/src/burnout3_car_physics.h
/src/burnout3_font.h
/src/burnout3_start_grid.h
/src/burnout3_track_paths.h
/src/burnout3_trackselect.h
/src/burnout3_traffic_data.h
/src/burnout3_vehicle_data.h

# Reference captures. Screenshots of the retail game are the game's artwork --
# cite a frame in the docs by all means, but do not commit one. That is why the
# frames docs/ and web/README.md cite are named rather than embedded.
/REFERENCE IMAGES/
*.xbe
*.iso
*.xiso

# THIRD-PARTY SOURCE IS FETCHED, NEVER COMMITTED -- three of them, same rule:
#   third_party/          Rockbox's libwma (LGPL), tools/fetch_wma.sh
#   android/third_party/  SDL2, SDL2_image, gl4es, android/fetch_deps.sh
#   web/third_party/      nothing any more; web/fetch_deps.sh says why
# Keeping the LGPL decoder out of this history is what keeps it separable --
# see THIRD_PARTY.md.
/third_party/
/web/third_party/

# Ghidra project database (regenerable by importing build/burnout3.elf)
/ghirda-manual.rep/
/ghirda-manual.gpr
/ghirda-manual.lock
/ghirda-manual.lock~

# Third-party clones with their own history
/ghidra-mcp/
/burnout-data-tool/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# recordings, scratch
/scratchpad/
*.mp4
